! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: without a declared publication cadence, readers cannot tell which version they are reading.
  + context: Minted as a marked self-derived fallback after A5's external-first search found living-document history but no statement of this specific version ambiguity.
  + IF:
    A recomputable paper exists in changing and frozen forms.
  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the source pattern: “Without a declared cadence, "which version am I reading" becomes unanswerable.” (source: futon3 library/ukrns/publication-cadence.flexiarg:15)
  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for publication-cadence mechanisms.
  + BECAUSE:
    The source class makes the circular provenance mechanically visible.
